  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best results (config_014: 0.713, config_024: 0.725) all use scvi_n200 + transformer aggregation in a multimodal setting. The earlier pca-based comparison (config_001 vs config_003) suggested multimodal helps by ~5pp, but we have no direct test of whether the image modality contributes when using the much stronger scvi_n200 encoder with transformer aggregation. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the image branch adds meaningful signal beyond what scvi_n200 + transformer already captures from the RNA profiles, or whether the apparent multimodal gain was an artifact of the weaker pca encoder. This experiment (config_019: rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) directly compares to config_014 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) by removing only the image modality and fusion, keeping RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation identical. If rna_only performs within ~1pp of the multimodal configs, the image branch is not worth its complexity and future effort should focus on RNA-side improvements; if it drops substantially, the image modality is confirmed as a key contributor and we should prioritize optimizing the image encoder and fusion. This is the highest-information experiment under budget because the answer fundamentally redirects the remaining search."
}

